tor retrieve_similar memory retrieval logic","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688q8_e9a85a8f98c9":{"observation":{"concepts":["system lifecycle"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Current timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:54:24.557Z"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688q8_e9a85a8f98c9","importance":1,"narrative":"The system has recorded a timestamped event marking the completion of a step in the execution lifecycle.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Routine system heartbeat","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.557Z","title":"System Timestamp Update","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688q8_b2523766720a":{"observation":{"concepts":["Memory Compression","Structured Data Extraction","XML Schema"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Role: Memory compression engine for an AI coding agent","Input: Timestamp 2026-06-26T16:54:24.558Z"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688q8_b2523766720a","importance":1,"narrative":"The system has been initialized with a specific instruction set for processing observations. It is ready to ingest and compress tool usage data into a standardized XML format for long-term memory management.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Memory compression engine activated","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.558Z","title":"System Initialization","type":"conversation"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688s2_21315eed098d":{"observation":{"concepts":["patch management","system lifecycle hooks"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:54:24.625Z","Event: patch_applied hook triggered"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688s2_21315eed098d","importance":3,"narrative":"A system hook named 'patch_applied' was triggered. This indicates a successful application of a patch or update to the system state.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"patch_applied event","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.625Z","title":"System Hook Triggered","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688s4_2cc56e977eca":{"observation":{"concepts":["system telemetry","session management"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Current timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:54:24.626Z","Hook context: session_status"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688s4_2cc56e977eca","importance":1,"narrative":"The system recorded a routine timestamp update within the session_status hook. This provides a temporal anchor for the current execution context.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Periodic system status check","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.626Z","title":"System Timestamp Update","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688v0_2118032906a3":{"observation":{"concepts":["system telemetry","parameter management"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:54:24.731Z","Hook: llm_params"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688v0_2118032906a3","importance":1,"narrative":"The system received a timestamped hook update regarding llm_params. This indicates a periodic update to the operational context or parameters used by the engine.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Metadata injection for memory compression","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.731Z","title":"System Context Update","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688xh_1d922c2fe48d":{"observation":{"concepts":["session management","event hooks"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:54:24.820Z","Event type: session_updated hook"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688xh_1d922c2fe48d","importance":2,"narrative":"A system-level hook 'session_updated' was triggered, indicating a change in the current session state. This event typically follows an update to user authentication or session metadata.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"System hook: session_updated","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.820Z","title":"Session Update Triggered","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv688z0_1257e3b5a52e":{"observation":{"concepts":["input validation","data stream processing"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["The input received was a timestamp and a hook identifier \"session_diff\"","The input failed to provide an actual tool usage observation to compress"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv688z0_1257e3b5a52e","importance":1,"narrative":"The system received a raw timestamp and hook identifier without any actionable tool observation content. This prevents the compression engine from performing its extraction task.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Error processing session_diff hook","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:24.827Z","title":"Invalid Input Format Error","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv68cp6_c568af877642":{"observation":{"concepts":["e2e testing","pytest","streaming response parsing","memory persistence"],"confidence":1,"facts":["pytest executed: tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","2 tests passed, 2 tests failed","Failure in test_chat_stream_persists_memory: expected 'Building the answer now...' in response.text","Failure in test_memory_recall_after_chat: expected 'Nexi response' in response content"],"files":["tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv68cp6_c568af877642","importance":5,"narrative":"Ran the end-to-end chat test suite to verify recent fixes. Two regression failures were identified in streaming persistence and memory recall functionality.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Executing pytest for nexi_chat_e2e.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:29.704Z","title":"Run e2e chat tests","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv68lxu_036930f0601f":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector similarity search","episodic memory retrieval","refactoring"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Removed logic that performed manual dictionary construction for memories when embedding is None","The method now focuses on initializing search_query instead of handling full retrieval logic within this block","Target file: /Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv68lxu_036930f0601f","importance":5,"narrative":"The retrieve_similar method was refactored to remove a large block of manual dictionary construction previously used when embedding was None. This simplifies the method's responsibility, likely delegating the heavy lifting to a more appropriate part of the retrieval pipeline.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Simplified implementation of retrieve_similar method","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:41.679Z","title":"Refactor retrieve_similar in pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv68rdz_0cc97f52b31b":{"observation":{"concepts":["Vector Search Fallback","Data Normalization","PostgreSQL Episodic Memory"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Modified retrieve_similar to handle cases where both embedding and query_text are missing.","Added fallback to get_memories when no search vector/text is provided.","Implemented explicit mapping of metadata fields (id, timestamp, type, raw_text, etc.) in the fallback result set.","Added logic to sort fallback memories by creation date and limit to top_k."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv68rdz_0cc97f52b31b","importance":5,"narrative":"The retrieval method was updated to provide a fallback mechanism. If no search criteria are provided, the system now fetches recent memories directly from the database, ensuring a graceful degradation of search functionality.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Enhanced retrieval logic for embedding-less queries","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:48.742Z","title":"Update retrieve_similar in pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv68unh_3266183bd93d":{"observation":{"concepts":["Server-Sent Events (SSE)","End-to-end testing","JSON stream parsing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Updated /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","Changed direct string assertion to iterative parsing of \"data: \" prefixed lines","Added logic to strip \"data: [DONE]\" from the stream processing"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv68unh_3266183bd93d","importance":5,"narrative":"The test was updated to correctly parse Server-Sent Events (SSE) in the chat response. Instead of checking the raw text, it now iterates through the stream, extracts JSON payloads from 'data: ' lines, and aggregates the content parts for assertion.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Refactor assertion to handle SSE (Server-Sent Events) format","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:54:52.971Z","title":"Update e2e test for streaming response parsing","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv690r0_b6b3cd7575d8":{"observation":{"concepts":["e2e testing","pytest","fastapi","asyncio","chat memory persistence"],"confidence":1,"facts":["3 out of 4 tests in tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py failed.","Failed tests: test_chat_roundtrip, test_chat_stream_persists_memory, test_memory_recall_after_chat.","Passed test: test_chat_injection_guard_rejects.","The failure in test_chat_roundtrip occurred during a POST request to /nexi/chat."],"files":["tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv690r0_b6b3cd7575d8","importance":6,"narrative":"Running the end-to-end test suite for the Nexi chat module revealed significant regressions or bugs in the core chat functionality, specifically affecting roundtrip communication, memory persistence, and memory recall. Only the injection guard test passed.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Running pytest for nexi_chat_e2e.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:00.873Z","title":"E2E Test Failures in Nexi Chat","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv69cgt_759467e3f5c7":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector search logic","episodic memory retrieval","Python async method refactoring"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Modified `retrieve_similar` method to decouple embedding check from query text check.","When `embedding` is None, it now defaults to returning recent memories regardless of `query_text` presence, simplifying the logic flow."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv69cgt_759467e3f5c7","importance":5,"narrative":"The code was refactored to clean up the conditional branching inside `retrieve_similar`. This ensures that if no embedding is provided, the function returns recent memories directly, avoiding redundant search query initialization.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Streamline conditional branch for embedding-based search","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:16.059Z","title":"Refactor retrieve_similar logic in pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv69f1d_523dcc52b939":{"observation":{"concepts":["Context Assembly","Knowledge Graph Retrieval","Episodic Memory","Entity Extraction","Multi-modal sensory buffer"],"confidence":1,"facts":["AssembledContext dataclass stores system prompts, recent turns, episodic memories, entity/relationship context, and sensory perceptions.","assemble_context function aggregates data from working_memory, pg_episodic (vector store), graph_store, relationship_store, and sensory_buffer.","Uses regex-based entity extraction from raw input to query the knowledge graph.","Integrates proactivity engine messages into the system prompt if available."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/context_assembler.py"],"id":"obs_mqv69f1d_523dcc52b939","importance":6,"narrative":"Read the context_assembler.py file to understand how the system builds the LLM prompt from various memory and sensory sources. This is a central component of the Nexi pipeline for multi-modal context injection.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Inspecting the core context assembly pipeline","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:19.392Z","title":"Read context_assembler.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv69r4s_85895c6b7664":{"observation":{"concepts":["database schema","metadata structure","agentmemory API"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Memory object keys: ['metadata', 'document', 'embedding', 'id']","Memory object does not contain 'created_at' at top level","Metadata contains 'raw_text', 'created_at', 'summary', and 'updated_at'","'raw_text' is nested inside the metadata dictionary"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv69r4s_85895c6b7664","importance":4,"narrative":"Ran a Python script to probe the database schema of the agentmemory module. Confirmed that top-level memory objects use a specific structure and that temporal metadata is stored within the metadata dict rather than the top-level object.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Verifying structure of retrieved memories in agentmemory module","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:35.065Z","title":"Inspect agentmemory schema","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv69w39_c69129181666":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory retrieval","data schema migration","dictionary access"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Changed sorting key from m.get('created_at', '') to m.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"created_at\", \"\")","Reflects a change in the schema where created_at is now nested inside a metadata object"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv69w39_c69129181666","importance":5,"narrative":"The memory retrieval logic was updated to correctly access the timestamp within a new metadata dictionary structure. This ensures compatibility with the updated memory storage format.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Adjusted memory sorting to access created_at within metadata dictionary","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:41.491Z","title":"Update memory retrieval key path","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6a9vg_5e7075d8fd1e":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory retrieval","timestamp sorting","vector embeddings"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Ran a Python script to create 3 memories and verify sorting by created_at timestamp.","Verified that the sorting logic correctly retrieves memories in descending order of created_at.","The memory objects include metadata with 'updated_at' and 'created_at' timestamps."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/bin/python"],"id":"obs_mqv6a9vg_5e7075d8fd1e","importance":4,"narrative":"Executed a bash command to run a Python debug script. The script confirmed that memories can be retrieved and sorted by their creation timestamp using the agentmemory API.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Debugging created_at sort order in agentmemory","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:55:59.353Z","title":"Verify agentmemory sorting logic","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6agwy_cd44f2b76904":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector database filtering","metadata querying","Python function inspection"],"confidence":1,"facts":["get_memories function accepts category, sort_order, contains_text, filter_metadata, n_results, include_embeddings, and novel.","Default sort_order is \"desc\".","Supports filtering via $contains for text and $eq for metadata equality.","Implementation uses get_client().get_or_create_collection(category) to access collections."],"files":[".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6agwy_cd44f2b76904","importance":4,"narrative":"The user executed a bash command to grep and inspect the source code of the get_memories function in the agentmemory package to understand its signature and filtering capabilities.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Analyzing implementation details and ordering logic in agentmemory/main.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:08.479Z","title":"Inspect agentmemory get_memories implementation","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6amss_478c0e75595d":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory episodic retrieval","timestamp-based sorting","agent memory management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Total of 9 episodes found in memory.","Python script verified that manual sorting by 'created_at' timestamp in descending order works as expected.","The 'get_memories' function returns episodes that are not natively sorted by timestamp in the initial retrieval."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems"],"id":"obs_mqv6amss_478c0e75595d","importance":4,"narrative":"Executed a python script to inspect the order of episodes retrieved via the agentmemory API. The test confirmed that episodes need explicit sorting by 'created_at' to achieve descending chronological order.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Verifying chronological sorting of episodes in test environment","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:16.107Z","title":"Debug agentmemory episode ordering","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6b0v4_3b4e0591e127":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector similarity search","episodic memory retrieval","metadata extraction","cosine similarity calculation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The `retrieve_similar` method handles both embedding-based and text-based queries.","If embedding is None, it falls back to `get_memories` with a timestamp-based sort.","If query_text is provided, it uses `search_memory` and calculates similarity as (1.0 - distance).","The method filters out archived memories and applies a `min_score` threshold.","Returned objects include structured metadata: importance, recall_count, decay_score, and timestamp."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/bin/python"],"id":"obs_mqv6b0v4_3b4e0591e127","importance":4,"narrative":"Executed a bash command to inspect the source code of `PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar`. This confirms the logic for similarity calculation and metadata extraction used during memory retrieval.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Verify source code of the episodic memory retrieval method","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:34.334Z","title":"Inspect PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar Implementation","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6b5fk_e386df420e16":{"observation":{"concepts":["E2E testing","pytest","assertion error","memory recall validation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Test failed: tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py::test_memory_recall_after_chat","Assertion error: expected 'Nexi response' in content, but found 'Hello Nexi\\nHello! I'm Nexi, your local AI assistant.'","Environment: Python 3.13.5, pytest-9.1.1, macOS (darwin)"],"files":["tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6b5fk_e386df420e16","importance":5,"narrative":"Ran a specific end-to-end test to verify memory recall functionality after chat. The test failed because the expected string 'Nexi response' was missing from the assistant's output.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"pytest execution for Nexi chat memory recall","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:40.253Z","title":"Run failing E2E test: test_memory_recall_after_chat","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bc7l_3004ea8a84a7":{"observation":{"concepts":["Python top-level await","integration testing","episodic memory retrieval"],"confidence":0.65,"facts":[],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/bin/python"],"id":"obs_mqv6bc7l_3004ea8a84a7","importance":1,"narrative":"A debug script designed to test the memory recall flow failed because it attempted to use 'await' in the global scope of the Python interpreter. This prevented the execution of the integration test for the Postgres episodic store and Nexi gateway.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Attempted to use await at top-level in a python script","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:49.037Z","title":"SyntaxError in debug script","type":"error"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bgwd_f653e5a82f8d":{"observation":{"concepts":["e2e testing","ChromaDB debugging","API response verification"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added `get_memories` from `agentmemory` to inspect ChromaDB contents during test execution.","Added debug print statements for episode count and recent episode metadata.","Added debug printing for the contents of the recall API response."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bgwd_f653e5a82f8d","importance":5,"narrative":"The end-to-end test for Nexi chat was updated to include debug-level logging. This allows developers to verify the state of the ChromaDB vector store and the specific content being returned by the recall endpoint during test runs.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Enhancing test visibility into ChromaDB and recall response","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:56:55.106Z","title":"Update e2e test with debug logging for memory recall","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bm1m_34266a17657f":{"observation":{"concepts":["E2E testing","Vector database retrieval","ChromaDB","Context window management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Test `test_memory_recall_after_chat` passed successfully.","ChromaDB contains 10 total episodes.","Recall search returned 5 relevant results.","Retrieved context includes both prior chat messages and specific recent interactions."],"files":["tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bm1m_34266a17657f","importance":5,"narrative":"Ran a specific end-to-end test to verify the AI's ability to recall chat history from ChromaDB. The test passed, confirming that the vector database correctly retrieves previous conversation turns during the chat session.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Executing pytest for Nexi chat memory integration","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:01.783Z","title":"Run E2E test: memory recall after chat","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bq7y_ae2c7e967421":{"observation":{"concepts":["debugging cleanup","end-to-end testing"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Removed debug prints that iterated through ChromaDB episodes","Removed logging of raw_text and created_at timestamps from episode metadata"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bq7y_ae2c7e967421","importance":3,"narrative":"The test script was updated to remove verbose debug printing of retrieved memory episodes from ChromaDB. This cleans up the test output while maintaining the core logic for recalling messages.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Cleaning up debug logging in end-to-end test","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:07.195Z","title":"Remove debug print statements in test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bswd_1f1d3fe7044a":{"observation":{"concepts":["e2e testing","test cleanup"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Removed print statements that logged recall result length and content snippets.","Reduced noise in test output during execution."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bswd_1f1d3fe7044a","importance":3,"narrative":"The edit cleaned up the test file by removing debug print statements that were used for manual verification of response contents. This streamlines the test output for cleaner CI/CD logs.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Removed verbose debug print statements from test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:10.668Z","title":"Simplify debug printing in e2e test","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bwul_8aff4c309261":{"observation":{"concepts":["end-to-end testing","pytest","chat stream persistence","prompt injection defense","long-term memory retrieval"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Command: pytest tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","All 4 tests passed successfully","Tests covered: chat roundtrip, stream persistence, injection guard, and memory recall","Environment: Python 3.13.5, macOS (darwin)"],"files":["tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bwul_8aff4c309261","importance":5,"narrative":"The full e2e test suite for the Nexi chat functionality was executed. All four critical test cases passed, confirming that chat flows, memory persistence, and security guards are functioning as expected.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Executed pytest suite for nexi_chat e2e tests","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:15.788Z","title":"Run end-to-end chat tests","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bzsq_0c858e5a7d16":{"observation":{"concepts":["workflow orchestration","lifecycle management"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Timestamp: 2026-06-26T16:57:19.608Z","Hook type: task_completed"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv6bzsq_0c858e5a7d16","importance":3,"narrative":"The system has emitted a task_completed hook, signaling the conclusion of a specific processing unit or workflow. This indicates the current execution context has reached a predefined milestone or end state.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"System-level event indicating task finalization","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:19.608Z","title":"Task Completion Notification","type":"task"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6bzsw_cec9afdd184a":{"observation":{"concepts":["refactoring","state management","test automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Completed refactor of app.state.X to app.X in nexi_gateway.py","Completed updating tests to match new app.X pattern","Completed unit test suite (9 tests) and e2e integration tests","Ongoing task: running full combined test suite"],"files":["nexi_gateway.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6bzsw_cec9afdd184a","importance":5,"narrative":"The refactoring task involving changing the state access pattern from app.state.X to app.X is nearing completion. Most individual components and integration tests have passed, with only the final combined test suite remaining in progress.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Progress tracking for refactoring nexi_gateway.py and associated tests","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:19.612Z","title":"Update Todo List: Refactor app.state.X to app.X","type":"task"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6c1ll_a01a0a6041ec":{"observation":{"concepts":["end-to-end testing","regression testing","pytest","memory persistence"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Ran 13 tests in total using pytest","12 tests passed, 1 test failed","Failure: test_memory_recall_after_chat in tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py","AssertionError: 'Nexi response' not found in expected output string"],"files":["tests/test_nexi_gateway.py","tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6c1ll_a01a0a6041ec","importance":5,"narrative":"Executed the test suite for the Nexi gateway and chat components. A regression or bug was detected in the end-to-end chat flow where memory recall fails after a chat session.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"pytest execution for nexi_gateway and nexi_chat","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:21.943Z","title":"Run Nexi Gateway and Chat E2E tests","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6ce98_d62b2227302a":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector similarity retrieval","embedding search optimization","episodic memory retrieval"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py: changed n_results from top_k to max(50, top_k * 10)"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6ce98_d62b2227302a","importance":5,"narrative":"The retrieval method was updated to fetch a significantly larger set of potential matches (either 50 or 10x top_k) before filtering, likely to improve recall during similarity searches.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"Modified similarity retrieval to use a larger buffer for initial memory fetching","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:38.346Z","title":"Update retrieval logic in pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6cj9l_dd774c7bfc21":{"observation":{"concepts":["end-to-end testing","prompt injection guards","memory persistence","pytest"],"confidence":1,"facts":["All 13 tests passed successfully","Tests covered gateway prompt building, caching, injection guards, and memory persistence","Environment: Python 3.13.5, pytest-9.1.1"],"files":["tests/test_nexi_gateway.py","tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py"],"id":"obs_mqv6cj9l_dd774c7bfc21","importance":5,"narrative":"Executed the full test suite for the Nexi gateway and chat E2E modules. All tests passed, confirming functionality of system prompt caching, injection guards, and memory recall/persistence features.","sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","subtitle":"pytest execution for nexi_gateway.py and nexi_chat_e2e.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:44.838Z","title":"Run Nexi Gateway and Chat E2E Test Suite","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv6cr7e_4ed36c16a6e5":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv6cr7e_4ed36c16a6e5","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_00_63Hy2Ocgvea1JnwoEb4l3375","duration_ms":92,"metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","tool_input":"{\"content\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set `app = request.app.state` then accessed `app.state.kv_cache`, but `app` IS the state already. This caused `app.state` to auto-create fresh MagicMocks.\\n\\n2. **`PlainTextResponse` for `/nexi/system-prompt`** — FastAPI wraps `str` return in JSON quotes by default. Added `response_class=PlainTextResponse`.\\n\\n3. **`PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar` normalization** — When `embedding is None`, raw ChromaDB results have `raw_text` inside `metadata` dict, not at top level. Fixed to normalize output + sort by `metadata.created_at`. Also increased batch fetch from `n_results=top_k` to `n_results=max(50, top_k*10)` to avoid ChromaDB's limit filtering out recent entries.\\n\\n4. **Stream test mock chain** — `mock_client_instance.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `stream.__aenter__`) and `MagicMock()` not `AsyncMock()` for stream response mock.\\n\\nAll 13 tests pass (9 unit + 4 e2e).\",\"type\":\"bug\",\"project\":\"xnchSystems\",\"files\":\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py,xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py,tests/test_nexi_gateway.py,tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py\",\"concepts\":\"nexi_gateway, FastAPI, testing, app.state, mocking, ChromaDB, PgEpisodicStore\"}","tool_name":"agentmemory_memory_save","tool_output":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"nexi_gateway\",\"FastAPI\",\"testing\",\"app.state\",\"mocking\",\"ChromaDB\",\"PgEpisodicStore\"],\"content\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set `app = request.app.state` then accessed `app.state.kv_cache`, but `app` IS the state already. This caused `app.state` to auto-create fresh MagicMocks.\\n\\n2. **`PlainTextResponse` for `/nexi/system-prompt`** — FastAPI wraps `str` return in JSON quotes by default. Added `response_class=PlainTextResponse`.\\n\\n3. **`PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar` normalization** — When `embedding is None`, raw ChromaDB results have `raw_text` inside `metadata` dict, not at top level. Fixed to normalize output + sort by `metadata.created_at`. Also increased batch fetch from `n_results=top_k` to `n_results=max(50, top_k*10)` to avoid ChromaDB's limit filtering out recent entries.\\n\\n4. **Stream test mock chain** — `mock_client_instance.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `stream.__aenter__`) and `MagicMock()` not `AsyncMock()` for stream response mock.\\n\\nAll 13 tests pass (9 unit + 4 e2e).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:57:55.067Z\",\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv6cr5q_4e3e095e5a1c\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set \",\"type\":\"bug\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:57:55.067Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}"},"sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:57:55.128Z","toolInput":"{\"content\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set `app = request.app.state` then accessed `app.state.kv_cache`, but `app` IS the state already. This caused `app.state` to auto-create fresh MagicMocks.\\n\\n2. **`PlainTextResponse` for `/nexi/system-prompt`** — FastAPI wraps `str` return in JSON quotes by default. Added `response_class=PlainTextResponse`.\\n\\n3. **`PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar` normalization** — When `embedding is None`, raw ChromaDB results have `raw_text` inside `metadata` dict, not at top level. Fixed to normalize output + sort by `metadata.created_at`. Also increased batch fetch from `n_results=top_k` to `n_results=max(50, top_k*10)` to avoid ChromaDB's limit filtering out recent entries.\\n\\n4. **Stream test mock chain** — `mock_client_instance.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `stream.__aenter__`) and `MagicMock()` not `AsyncMock()` for stream response mock.\\n\\nAll 13 tests pass (9 unit + 4 e2e).\",\"type\":\"bug\",\"project\":\"xnchSystems\",\"files\":\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py,xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py,tests/test_nexi_gateway.py,tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py\",\"concepts\":\"nexi_gateway, FastAPI, testing, app.state, mocking, ChromaDB, PgEpisodicStore\"}","toolName":"agentmemory_memory_save","toolOutput":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"nexi_gateway\",\"FastAPI\",\"testing\",\"app.state\",\"mocking\",\"ChromaDB\",\"PgEpisodicStore\"],\"content\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set `app = request.app.state` then accessed `app.state.kv_cache`, but `app` IS the state already. This caused `app.state` to auto-create fresh MagicMocks.\\n\\n2. **`PlainTextResponse` for `/nexi/system-prompt`** — FastAPI wraps `str` return in JSON quotes by default. Added `response_class=PlainTextResponse`.\\n\\n3. **`PgEpisodicStore.retrieve_similar` normalization** — When `embedding is None`, raw ChromaDB results have `raw_text` inside `metadata` dict, not at top level. Fixed to normalize output + sort by `metadata.created_at`. Also increased batch fetch from `n_results=top_k` to `n_results=max(50, top_k*10)` to avoid ChromaDB's limit filtering out recent entries.\\n\\n4. **Stream test mock chain** — `mock_client_instance.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `stream.__aenter__`) and `MagicMock()` not `AsyncMock()` for stream response mock.\\n\\nAll 13 tests pass (9 unit + 4 e2e).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:57:55.067Z\",\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_chat_e2e.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv6cr5q_4e3e095e5a1c\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"Fixed 3 bugs in nexi_gateway tests:\\n\\n1. **`app.state.X` → `app.X`** — Route set \",\"type\":\"bug\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:57:55.067Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv6drz2_574c9b168567":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv6drz2_574c9b168567","raw":{"agent":"build","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Explicitly save an insight, decision, or learning to agentmemory for future sessions. Wraps the `memory_save` MCP tool.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/remember [what to remember]\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Analyze what needs to be remembered — extract the core insight, decision, or fact.\n2. Extract 2-5 searchable concepts (lowercased keyword phrases). Prefer specific terms (\"jwt-refresh-rotation\" over \"auth\").\n3. Extract relevant file paths the memory references.\n4. Call `memory_save` with:\n   - `content` — full text to remember (preserve user's phrasing)\n   - `concepts` — extracted concept list\n   - `files` — extracted file list (empty array if none)\n   - `type` — choose from: pattern, preference, architecture, bug, workflow, fact\n5. Confirm the save and show the concepts tagged so the user knows retrieval terms.","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:58:42.780Z","userPrompt":"Explicitly save an insight, decision, or learning to agentmemory for future sessions. Wraps the `memory_save` MCP tool.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/remember [what to remember]\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Analyze what needs to be remembered — extract the core insight, decision, or fact.\n2. Extract 2-5 searchable concepts (lowercased keyword phrases). Prefer specific terms (\"jwt-refresh-rotation\" over \"auth\").\n3. Extract relevant file paths the memory references.\n4. Call `memory_save` with:\n   - `content` — full text to remember (preserve user's phrasing)\n   - `concepts` — extracted concept list\n   - `files` — extracted file list (empty array if none)\n   - `type` — choose from: pattern, preference, architecture, bug, workflow, fact\n5. Confirm the save and show the concepts tagged so the user knows retrieval terms."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv6dxly_95b61352432d":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv6dxly_95b61352432d","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_00_MZndTmCTKQLLKhuFS3VC6385","duration_ms":100,"metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","tool_input":"{\"content\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object), all subsequent accesses to `app.state.X` create fresh MagicMock children in tests, losing pre-set attributes. Fix: access `app.X` directly (no `.state` indirection) since `app` is already the state object.\\n\\nChromaDB/agentmemory stores content (`raw_text`, `summary`) inside the `metadata` dict, not at top level. `get_memories()` returns raw results with `.metadata.raw_text` not `.raw_text`. Must normalize or access `ep[\\\"metadata\\\"][\\\"raw_text\\\"]`. Also, `get_memories()` only fetches `n_results` items by ChromaDB internal ordering, not necessarily the most recent — batch higher then sort by `metadata.created_at`.\\n\\nFor httpx.AsyncClient mock chains with `stream()`, use `mock_client.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `mock_client.stream.__aenter__`) since calling `stream(...)` creates a `return_value` child mock. Stream response mock should be `MagicMock` not `AsyncMock` for `status_code` attribute.\",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"concepts\":\"fastapi route state mocking, app.state children mock, agentmemory chromadb metadata normalization, httpx asyncclient stream mock, chromadb get_memories ordering\",\"files\":\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py,xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py,tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"}","tool_name":"agentmemory_memory_save","tool_output":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"fastapi route state mocking\",\"app.state children mock\",\"agentmemory chromadb metadata normalization\",\"httpx asyncclient stream mock\",\"chromadb get_memories ordering\"],\"content\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object), all subsequent accesses to `app.state.X` create fresh MagicMock children in tests, losing pre-set attributes. Fix: access `app.X` directly (no `.state` indirection) since `app` is already the state object.\\n\\nChromaDB/agentmemory stores content (`raw_text`, `summary`) inside the `metadata` dict, not at top level. `get_memories()` returns raw results with `.metadata.raw_text` not `.raw_text`. Must normalize or access `ep[\\\"metadata\\\"][\\\"raw_text\\\"]`. Also, `get_memories()` only fetches `n_results` items by ChromaDB internal ordering, not necessarily the most recent — batch higher then sort by `metadata.created_at`.\\n\\nFor httpx.AsyncClient mock chains with `stream()`, use `mock_client.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `mock_client.stream.__aenter__`) since calling `stream(...)` creates a `return_value` child mock. Stream response mock should be `MagicMock` not `AsyncMock` for `status_code` attribute.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:58:49.999Z\",\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv6dxjp_13c643c6be69\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object\",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:58:49.999Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}"},"sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:58:50.084Z","toolInput":"{\"content\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object), all subsequent accesses to `app.state.X` create fresh MagicMock children in tests, losing pre-set attributes. Fix: access `app.X` directly (no `.state` indirection) since `app` is already the state object.\\n\\nChromaDB/agentmemory stores content (`raw_text`, `summary`) inside the `metadata` dict, not at top level. `get_memories()` returns raw results with `.metadata.raw_text` not `.raw_text`. Must normalize or access `ep[\\\"metadata\\\"][\\\"raw_text\\\"]`. Also, `get_memories()` only fetches `n_results` items by ChromaDB internal ordering, not necessarily the most recent — batch higher then sort by `metadata.created_at`.\\n\\nFor httpx.AsyncClient mock chains with `stream()`, use `mock_client.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `mock_client.stream.__aenter__`) since calling `stream(...)` creates a `return_value` child mock. Stream response mock should be `MagicMock` not `AsyncMock` for `status_code` attribute.\",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"concepts\":\"fastapi route state mocking, app.state children mock, agentmemory chromadb metadata normalization, httpx asyncclient stream mock, chromadb get_memories ordering\",\"files\":\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py,xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py,tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"}","toolName":"agentmemory_memory_save","toolOutput":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"fastapi route state mocking\",\"app.state children mock\",\"agentmemory chromadb metadata normalization\",\"httpx asyncclient stream mock\",\"chromadb get_memories ordering\"],\"content\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object), all subsequent accesses to `app.state.X` create fresh MagicMock children in tests, losing pre-set attributes. Fix: access `app.X` directly (no `.state` indirection) since `app` is already the state object.\\n\\nChromaDB/agentmemory stores content (`raw_text`, `summary`) inside the `metadata` dict, not at top level. `get_memories()` returns raw results with `.metadata.raw_text` not `.raw_text`. Must normalize or access `ep[\\\"metadata\\\"][\\\"raw_text\\\"]`. Also, `get_memories()` only fetches `n_results` items by ChromaDB internal ordering, not necessarily the most recent — batch higher then sort by `metadata.created_at`.\\n\\nFor httpx.AsyncClient mock chains with `stream()`, use `mock_client.stream.return_value.__aenter__` (not `mock_client.stream.__aenter__`) since calling `stream(...)` creates a `return_value` child mock. Stream response mock should be `MagicMock` not `AsyncMock` for `status_code` attribute.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:58:49.999Z\",\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv6dxjp_13c643c6be69\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"When FastAPI routes use `app = request.app.state` (snapshotting the state object\",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T16:58:49.999Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv6e0kz_8f7d38e3c5fc":{"observation":{"hookType":"command_executed","id":"obs_mqv6e0kz_8f7d38e3c5fc","raw":{"arguments":"","name":"remember"},"sessionId":"ses_0fb2fd363ffe1wHxMGJQdoOLLx","timestamp":"2026-06-26T16:58:53.939Z"},"type":"raw"}}��␀ ��